<title>FRANCE: Technip signs UAE cement plant deal.</title>
<headline>Technip signs UAE cement plant deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French engineering company Technip has signed a contract to build and equip a cement factory in the United Arab Emirates, valued at around 900 million francs, a company spokeswoman said on Monday.</p>
<p>The contract for a turnkey installation to be delivered at the Khor Khwair site was signed on Saturday with local partner Ras Al Khaimah Cement Co, she said. The factory will have annual output of one million tonnes, with some production intended for the local market and some for export.</p>
<p>French cement company Lafarge said it will be a consultant and manage the factory.</p>
<p>Lafarge will also train local employees and will market &quot;a significant part of the output,&quot; a Lafarge spokesman said.</p>
</text>
